commit 22182c33f9441ff0a6dd6fb44beff497fb37d368
Author: Timothy Middelkoop <tmiddelkoop@internet2.edu>
Date:   Wed Apr 29 00:56:56 2026 -0500

    docs: port installation guide from LaTeX to Markdown/Jinja2
    
    Backport the Markdown/Jinja2 documentation system from the 4.x
    branch, adapted for EL9 and the OpenHPC 3.x package set.
    
      - Seed mkdoc.py, templates/, and config/ from the 4.x branch
      - Adapt distro configs for EL9 (Rocky 9, AlmaLinux 9),
        openEuler 22.03, and Leap 15
      - Add Warewulf v3 provisioner support (wwsh/wwmkchroot/wwvnfs)
      - Add OpenPBS scheduler support alongside Slurm
      - Add OpenEuler + OpenPBS via Warewulf v4
      - Build all 28 recipes across Warewulf v3/v4, Slurm/OpenPBS,
        x86_64/aarch64 combinations
      - Replace LaTeX-based RPM build with Markdown/Jinja2 system
        (BuildRequires: yq, python3, python3-jinja2, python3-pyyaml)
      - Build docs-ohpc as noarch on EL only; skip openEuler/Leap CI
      - Regenerate package manifests from OpenHPC 3.4 staging repos
      - Fix DHCPd configuration for EL9
      - Fix Python 3.9 compatibility in mkdoc.py
      - Fix warewulf3 package name, modernize commands, fix VM boot
    
    Signed-off-by: Timothy Middelkoop <tmiddelkoop@internet2.edu>
    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
