+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/base-os/ssh-key.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/base-os/ssh-key.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b4e957353
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/base-os/ssh-key.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Generate SSH Key Pair
+
+An SSH key pair on the *head node* enables passwordless access to compute nodes
+and is useful for automating cluster configuration tasks.
+{% if is_confluent %}
+It is also required by the Confluent provisioner for node deployment.
+{% endif %}
+If an ed25519 key does not already exist, generate one:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+```bash
+[[ -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ]] || ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N ''
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+::: {.tip}
+**Note:** The key is generated without a passphrase (`-N ''`) to allow
+unattended use in scripts and automated workflows. Ensure that access to the
+head node is appropriately restricted.
+:::
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/base-os/time.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/base-os/time.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..185649338
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/base-os/time.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+## Configure NTP
+
+HPC systems rely on synchronized clocks throughout the system and the NTP
+protocol can be used to facilitate this synchronization. To enable NTP services
+on the head node with a specific server `${ntp_server}`, and allow this server
+to serve as a local time server for the cluster, issue the following:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Enable NTP services on head node -->
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} chrony
+systemctl enable chronyd.service
+echo "local stratum 10" >> /etc/chrony.conf
+echo "server ${ntp_server}" >> /etc/chrony.conf
+echo "allow all" >> /etc/chrony.conf
+systemctl restart chronyd
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+::: {.tip}
+**Note:** Note that the "allow all" option specified for the chrony time daemon
+allows all servers on the local network to be able to synchronize with the head
+node. Alternatively, you can restrict access to fixed IP ranges and an example
+config line allowing access to a local class B subnet is as follows:
+
+```bash
+allow 192.168.0.0/16
+```
+:::
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/boot/boot-computes.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/boot/boot-computes.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..04d0e16d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/boot/boot-computes.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+## Boot Compute Nodes
+
+At this point, the *head node* should be able to boot the newly defined compute
+nodes. Assuming that the compute node BIOS settings are configured to boot over
+PXE, all that is required to initiate the provisioning process is to power cycle
+each of the desired hosts using IPMI access. The following commands use the
+`ipmitool` utility to initiate power resets on each of the four compute hosts.
+Note that the utility requires that the `IPMI_PASSWORD` environment variable be
+set with the local BMC password in order to work interactively.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Boot compute nodes -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set has_ipmi -->
+```bash
+for ((i=0; i<num_computes; i++)) ; do
+  ipmitool -E -I lanplus -H "${c_bmc[$i]}" -U "${bmc_username}" \
+    -P "${bmc_password}" chassis power reset
+done
+```
+<!-- ohpc_else -->
+<!-- ohpc_command # In-band communication to reset nodes     -->
+<!-- ohpc_command for ((i=0; i<num_computes; i++)) ; do      -->
+<!-- ohpc_command   echo "#<<< ohpc_reset:$i,${c_name[$i]},${c_bmc[$i]} >>>#" -->
+<!-- ohpc_command done                                       -->
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+Once kicked off, the boot process should take less than 5 minutes (depending on
+BIOS post times) and you can verify that the compute hosts are available via
+ssh, or via parallel ssh tools to multiple hosts. For example, to run a command
+on the newly imaged compute hosts using `pdsh`, execute the following:
+
+```bash
+pdsh -w ${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}] uptime
+c1  05:03am  up   0:02,  0 users,  load average: 0.20, 0.13, 0.05
+c2  05:03am  up   0:02,  0 users,  load average: 0.20, 0.14, 0.06
+c3  05:03am  up   0:02,  0 users,  load average: 0.19, 0.15, 0.06
+c4  05:03am  up   0:02,  0 users,  load average: 0.15, 0.12, 0.05
+```
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/boot/wait.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/boot/wait.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ff6717be1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/boot/wait.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Allow for optional sleep to wait for provisioning to complete -->
