diff --git a/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/mpi.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/mpi.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..3a088be95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/mpi.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@
+## MPI Stacks
+
+For MPI development and runtime support, OpenHPC provides pre-packaged builds
+for a variety of MPI families and transport layers. Currently available options
+and their applicability to various network transports are summarized in the
+Available MPI variants table below.  The command that follows installs a
+starting set of MPI families that are compatible with both ethernet and
+high-speed fabrics.
+
+{% if is_x86_64 %}
+**Table: Available MPI variants**
+
+|                       | Ethernet (TCP) | InfiniBand | Intel Omni-Path |
+|-----------------------|:--------------:|:----------:|:---------------:|
+| MPICH (ofi)           | ✓              | ✓          | ✓               |
+| MPICH (ucx)           | ✓              | ✓          | ✓               |
+| MVAPICH2              |                | ✓          |                 |
+| MVAPICH2 (psm2)       |                |            | ✓               |
+| OpenMPI (ofi/ucx)     | ✓              | ✓          | ✓               |
+
+{% else %}
+**Table: Available MPI builds**
+
+|                       | Ethernet (TCP) | InfiniBand |
+|-----------------------|:--------------:|:----------:|
+| MPICH                 | ✓              |            |
+| OpenMPI               | ✓              | ✓          |
+
+{% endif %}
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Install MPI Stacks -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_mpi_defaults -->
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} {{ openmpi_version }}-{% if is_slurm %}pmix-{% endif %}{{ gnu_version }}-ohpc mpich-ofi-{{ gnu_version }}-ohpc
+```
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+Note that OpenHPC 2.x introduces the use of two related transport layers for the
+MPICH and OpenMPI builds that support a variety of underlying fabrics:
+[UCX](https://www.openucx.org) (Unified Communication X) and
+[OFI](https://ofiwg.github.io/libfabric/) (OpenFabrics interfaces). In the case
+of OpenMPI, a monolithic build is provided which supports both transports and
+end-users can customize their runtime preferences with environment variables.
+For MPICH, two separate builds are provided and the example above highlighted
+installing the `ofi` variant.  However, the packaging is designed such that both
+versions can be installed simultaneously and users can switch between the two
+via normal module command semantics. Alternatively, a site can choose to install
+the `ucx` variant instead as a drop-in MPICH replacement:
+
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} mpich-ucx-{{ gnu_version }}-ohpc
+```
+
+In the case where both MPICH variants are installed, two modules will be visible
+in the end-user environment and an example of this configuration is highlighted
+is below.
+
+```bash
+module avail mpich
+
+-------------------- /opt/ohpc/pub/moduledeps/{{ gnu_version }}---------------------
+   mpich/3.4.3-ofi    mpich/3.4.3-ucx (D)
+```
+
+If your system includes InfiniBand and you enabled underlying support in
+[InfiniBand support](#optionally-add-infiniband-support-services-on-head-node)
+and [Enable Infiniband Drivers](#enable-infiniband-drivers), an additional
+MVAPICH2 family is available for use:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ib -->
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} mvapich2-{{ gnu_version }}-ohpc
+```
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+Alternatively, if your system includes Intel Omni-Path, use the (`psm2`) variant
+of MVAPICH2 instead:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_opa -->
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} mvapich2-psm2-{{ gnu_version }}-ohpc
+```
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+<!--
+https://github.com/openhpc/ohpc/issues/1273
+disabling until we can get pmix/openmpi/slurm to play nicely
+
+An additional OpenMPI build variant is listed in the Available MPI variants table which
+enables [PMIx](https://pmix.github.io/pmix/) job launch
+support for use with Slurm. This optional variant is
+available as `{{ openmpi_version }}-pmix-slurm-gnu9-ohpc`.
+-->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/oneapi-enabled-builds.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/oneapi-enabled-builds.md.j2
