diff --git a/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/third-party-libs.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/third-party-libs.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..0f9d22790
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/dev-tools/third-party-libs.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+::: {.tip}
+
+OpenHPC-provided 3rd party builds are configured to be installed into a common
+top-level repository so that they can be easily exported to desired hosts within
+the cluster. This common top-level path (`/opt/ohpc/pub`) was previously
+configured to be mounted on **compute** nodes in an earlier section, so the
+packages will be immediately available for use on the cluster after installation
+on the **head node**.
+:::
+
+For convenience, OpenHPC provides package aliases for these 3rd party libraries
+and utilities that can be used to install available libraries for use with the
+GNU compiler family toolchain. For parallel libraries, aliases are grouped by
+MPI family toolchain so that administrators can choose a subset should they
+favor a particular MPI stack. Please refer to the Package Manifest appendix for
+a more detailed listing of all available packages in each of these functional
+areas. To install all available package offerings within OpenHPC, issue the
+following:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Install 3rd Party Libraries and Tools -->
+```bash
+# Install 3rd party libraries/tools meta-packages built with GNU toolchain
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-serial-libs
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-io-libs
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-python-libs
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-runtimes
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
