+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_mpi_defaults -->
+```bash
+# Install parallel lib meta-packages for all available MPI toolchains
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-mpich-parallel-libs
+{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-{{ openmpi_version }}-parallel-libs
+```
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ib -->
+<!-- ohpc_command {{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-mvapich2-parallel-libs -->
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_opa -->
+<!-- ohpc_command {{ pkg_install }} ohpc-{{ gnu_version }}-mvapich2-parallel-libs -->
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/distro/el/repos.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/distro/el/repos.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..35196a82f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/distro/el/repos.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+## Enable EL Package Repositories
+
+In addition to the OpenHPC package repository, the *head node* also requires
+access to the standard base OS distro repositories in order to resolve necessary
+dependencies. For {{ distro_full_name }}, the requirements are to have access to
+the BaseOS, Appstream, Extras, CRB, and EPEL repositories for which mirrors are
+freely available online:
+
+{% if is_almalinux %}
+* AlmaLinux-9 (e.g.
+  [https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/9/](https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/9/))
+* EPEL 9 (e.g.
+  [http://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/9/](http://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/9/))
+{% elif is_rocky %}
+* Rocky-9 (e.g.
+  [http://download.rockylinux.org/pub/rocky/9/](http://download.rockylinux.org/pub/rocky/9/))
+* EPEL 9 (e.g.
+  [http://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/9/](http://download.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/9/))
+{% endif %}
+
+Although the public EPEL repository would be enabled automatically upon
+installation of the `ohpc-release` package, we install it now. Note that this
+does depend on the {{ distro_full_name }} Extras repository, which is shipped
+with {{ distro_full_name }} and is typically enabled by default.  In contrast,
+the CRB repository is typically disabled in a standard install, but can be
+enabled from EPEL as follows:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Install EPEL and enable CRB-->
+```bash
+dnf -y install epel-release dnf-plugins-core
+dnf config-manager --set-enabled crb
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/distro/openeuler/repos.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/distro/openeuler/repos.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..aaa132c92
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/distro/openeuler/repos.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+In addition to the OpenHPC package repository, the *head node* also requires
+access to the standard base OS distro repositories in order to resolve necessary
+dependencies. For {{ distro_full_name }}, the requirements are to have access to
+the OS, Everything, EPOL main, and EPOL update repositories. Note that the OS,
+Everything, and EPOL main repositories are typically enabled by default. To
+enable the EPOL update repository on {{ distro_full_name }}, you can run the
+following command:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Install EPOL -->
+
+```bash
+{{ pkg_add_repo }} {{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_server }}\
+/{{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_dir }}\
+/{{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_file }}
+{{ pkg_install }} openeuler-extra-repos
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+By default all repositories use
+[http://repo.openeuler.org](http://repo.openeuler.org). For better network speed
+it could be replaced with any of the mirrors listed
+[here](https://www.openeuler.org/en/mirror/list/).
