diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/dhcp-config.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/dhcp-config.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..aaa5421f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/dhcp-config.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Setup DHCP
+
+{{ provisioner_name }} uses CoreDHCP as the DHCP service to provide IP addresses
+to nodes. There is a default configuration in place that we need to overwrite.
+
+If your router address is different than the internal network address .254 you
+will need to change this file on your own. CoreDHCP has been configured to only
+provide addresses to nodes it knows. There are some extra [configuration
+changes](https://github.com/OpenCHAMI/deployment-recipes/blob/main/quickstart/DHCP.md)
+you can make to change that.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Configure DHCP -->
+```bash
+cat > /etc/openchami/configs/coredhcp.yaml <<EOF
+server4:
+ plugins:
+    - server_id: ${sms_ip}
+    - router: ${ipv4_gateway}
+    - dns: ${dns_servers}
+    - netmask: ${internal_netmask}
+    - coresmd: https://${sms_name}:8443 http://${sms_ip}:8081 \
+/root_ca/root_ca.crt 30s 1h false
+EOF
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/install.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/install.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..62dfefede
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/install.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Install OpenCHAMI
+
+To begin we need to add the OpenCHAMI RPM to the head node, by
+adding it to the list of available packages locally. This requires network
+access from the *head node* to the internet.  We then source
+`/etc/profile.d/openchami.sh` to update the shell.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Enable OpenCHAMI Repositories and Support -->
+```bash
+{{ pkg_install }} podman buildah ansible-core nfs-utils tcpdump tftp curl yq jq
+rpm --import \
+	https://github.com/OpenCHAMI/release/releases/download/\
+v{{ openchami_version }}/repo_public.asc
+{{ pkg_install }} \
+	https://github.com/OpenCHAMI/release/releases/download/\
+v{{ openchami_version }}/openchami-{{ openchami_version }}.rpm
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Source /etc/profile.d/openchami.sh -->
+```bash
+source /etc/profile.d/openchami.sh
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/intro.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/intro.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..335731190
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/intro.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+Installation is completed in a few parts. First we build the images that the
+*compute* nodes will boot off of. Then we configure the cloud-init steps to add
+a local account, mount remote file systems, and inject the munge key into the
+OS. OpenHPC components will be added to both the head node and compute nodes.
+The head node will get the components during install, and compute nodes will get
+them during image builds.
+
+OpenCHAMI uses an Infrastructure as Code tool called image-builder
+to translate YAML files to system images in layers to build out reusable file
+system layers like container images. This enables the rapid rebuild of images in
+smaller more usable and readable layers. OpenCHAMI uses SquashFS
+images over S3 to serve to nodes, and Container images through OCI.
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/node-discovery.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/node-discovery.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..9f090b51a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/node-discovery.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+## Node Discovery
+
+{{ provisioner_name }} can do dynamic discovery, but here we will do node
+discovery by YAML file. The YAML file can be imported by the discover command
+creating a way for adding nodes that do not have redfish capabilities, or when
+you just want to provide a list of nodes.
+
+Create the `nodes.yaml` file the static discovery will use to populate SMD.
+Also add the compute node names to `/etc/hosts` for SSH access.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Discovering Nodes -->
+```bash
+mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/admin/nodes
+nf=/opt/ohpc/admin/nodes/nodes.yaml
+
+## Add BMCs
+echo "bmcs:" > $nf
+for((i=0; i < $num_computes; i++)); do
+	nid=$((i+1))
+	printf -v mac '%02x:%02x' "$(((nid >> 8) & 0xff))" "$((nid & 0xff))"
+	cat >> $nf << EOF
+- xname: x1000c0s0b${nid}
+  ip: ${c_bmc[$i]}
+  mac: 02:00:00:00:${mac}
+EOF
+done
+
+## Add nodes
+echo "nodes:" >> $nf
+for((i=0; i < $num_computes; i++)); do
+	nid=$((i+1))
+	cat >> $nf << EOF
+- name: ${c_name[$i]}
+  nid: ${nid}
+  xname: x1000c0s0b${nid}n0
+  bmc: x1000c0s0b${nid}
+  groups:
+  - compute
+  interfaces:
+  - mac_addr: ${c_mac[$i]}
+    ip_addrs:
+    - name: internal
+      ip_addr: ${c_ip[$i]}
+EOF
+done
+
+## Add nodes to /etc/hosts
+for((i=0; i < $num_computes; i++)); do
+	echo "${c_ip[$i]} ${c_name[$i]}" >> /etc/hosts
+done
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+Now use the generated file to populate the SMD database.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Passing ochami the nodes -->
+```bash
+ochami discover static \
+	-f yaml -d @/opt/ohpc/admin/nodes/nodes.yaml
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+`ochami discover static` populates SMD components, EthernetInterfaces (under the correct
+node xname), and group membership from the `nodes.yaml` file in a single step.
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/noproxy.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/noproxy.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4a852ecc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/openchami/noproxy.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+## Setting no proxy
+
+{{ provisioner_name }} runs its own internal proxy for services which may not
+interact well if you run another httpd server. Here we set the no proxy variable
+to prevent lookups.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment OpenCHAMI No Proxy Settings -->
+```bash
+export additonal_no_proxy="${sms_name},opaal,opaal-idp,smd,smd-init,\
+hydra,cloud-init,acme-deploy,bss,haproxy,postgres,step-ca,configurator"
+if [ -z "$no_proxy" ]; then
+    export no_proxy="$additonal_no_proxy"
+else
+    export no_proxy="$no_proxy,$additonal_no_proxy"
+fi
+if [ -z "$NO_PROXY" ]; then
+    export NO_PROXY="$additonal_no_proxy"
+else
+    export NO_PROXY="$NO_PROXY,$additonal_no_proxy"
+fi
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
