--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-infiniband.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Finally, to add *optional* support for controlling IPoIB interfaces (see
+[Optionally add InfiniBand support services on *head
+node*](#optionally-add-infiniband-support-services-on-head-node)), OpenHPC
+includes a template file for Warewulf that can optionally be imported and used
+later to provision `ib0` network settings.
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ipoib -->
+```bash
+# Import the template file for the ib interface
+wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
+	/opt/ohpc/pub/examples/network/centos/ifcfg-ib0.ww \
+	/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/ifcfg-ib0.ww
+```
+<!-- ohpc_fi -->
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-ohpc.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-ohpc.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..943b35b12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-ohpc.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+## Add OpenHPC Components
+
+Next, we add additional components to include resource management client
+services, NTP support, and other additional packages to support the default
+OpenHPC environment. This process modifies the base provisioning image and will
+access the Base OS and OpenHPC repositories to resolve package install requests.
+
+The instructions below are designed to be copied and pasted all at once into a
+terminal.  Alternatively you can run `wwctl image shell {{ baseos }}` to "run"
+the node image interactively and run the commands one at a time, this method is
+recommended.
+
+We begin by installing a few common base packages:
+
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Add OpenHPC base components to compute image -->
+```bash
+
+# Install compute node base meta-package
+wwctl image exec --build=false {{ baseos }} -- /bin/bash -ex <<- EOF
+{% if is_el %}
+  dnf -y install epel-release
+{% elif is_openeuler %}
+  dnf -y config-manager --add-repo {{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_server }}\
+/{{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_dir }}\
+/{{ openeuler_ohpc_repo_file }}
+  dnf -y install openeuler-extra-repos
+{% endif %}
+  dnf -y install ohpc-base-compute
+EOF
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
+
+Now, we can include additional required components to the compute instance
+including resource manager client, NTP, and development environment modules
+support.
+
+Adding packages can be done by entering the image with `wwctl image shell`,
+`wwctl image exec`, or using a CHROOT.
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-openpbs.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-openpbs.md.j2
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..a6ea84e01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-openpbs.md.j2
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+<!-- ohpc_begin -->
+<!-- ohpc_comment Add OpenPBS and other components to compute instance -->
+```bash
+wwctl image exec --build=false {{ baseos }} -- /bin/bash -ex <<- EOF
+  # Add OpenPBS client support meta-package
+  dnf -y install openpbs-execution-ohpc
+
+  # Configure PBS server and initialize mom directory structure
+  sed -i "s/PBS_SERVER=\S\+/PBS_SERVER=${sms_name}/" /etc/pbs.conf
+  /opt/pbs/libexec/pbs_habitat
+  sed -i "s/\\\$clienthost \S\+/\\\$clienthost ${sms_name}/" \
+      /var/spool/pbs/mom_priv/config
+  echo "\\\$usecp *:/home /home" >> /var/spool/pbs/mom_priv/config
+
+  # Enable pbs service on boot
+  systemctl enable pbs
+
+  # Add Network Time Protocol (NTP) support
+  dnf -y install chrony
+
+  # Include modules user environment
+  dnf -y install lmod-ohpc
+EOF
+```
+<!-- ohpc_end -->
diff --git a/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-slurm.md.j2 b/docs/install/templates/provisioner/warewulf/compute-install-slurm.md.j2
